From 9621c5d16f3342474e767cb2dd305e17227e6af4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabrice Gasnier <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Nov 2021 18:10:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: handle suspended gadget when going to low power

When unplugging the cable, dwc2 detects a bus suspend, hence the driver
put the controller in one of the low power modes (clock gating, ppd).
Alternatively, the host may have suspended the bus.
When the user requests to go to low power, there's no choice but to
disconnect (or the host will go into troubles when resuming, due to
platform not able to respond).

So, in case the bus is suspended before going to low power mode,
dwc2_hsotg_suspend() will be a no-op.
When resuming, the controller registers may have been lost and
dwc2_hsotg_resume will also be a no-op. It's then not functional.
In such case the gadget needs to be properly suspended, so it
will be properly resumed later.

Signed-off-by: Fabrice Gasnier <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I7deb8aecbec1420060ee05a74c4fa0a5e7315a7d
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
index c34031556402..205642852c57 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
@@ -722,8 +722,25 @@ static int __maybe_unused dwc2_suspend(struct device *dev)
 		return 0;
 
 	is_device_mode = dwc2_is_device_mode(dwc2);
-	if (is_device_mode)
+	if (is_device_mode) {
+		/*
+		 * Handle the case when bus has been suspended prior to platform suspend.
+		 * As the lx_state is DWC2_L2, dwc2_hsotg_suspend() is then a no-op.
+		 * So need to exit clock gating first, so the gadget can be suspended and
+		 * resumed later on.
+		 */
+		if (dwc2->in_ppd) {
+			ret = dwc2_exit_partial_power_down(dwc2, 0, true);
+			if (ret)
+				dev_err(dwc2->dev, "exit power_down failed\n");
+		}
+
+		if (dwc2->params.power_down == DWC2_POWER_DOWN_PARAM_NONE &&
+		    dwc2->bus_suspended && !dwc2->params.no_clock_gating)
+			dwc2_gadget_exit_clock_gating(dwc2, 0);
+
 		dwc2_hsotg_suspend(dwc2);
+	}
 
 	dwc2_drd_suspend(dwc2);
 
-- 
